        "date_published": "2026-10-31T15:30:59+00:00",
        "description": "If the polls are to be believed, voters are feeling sore about rising grocery prices, the cost of gas and diesel and the unfinished military action against Iran. \n\nImmigration, once the President\u2019s strongest issue, is beginning to put strain on the coalition he built in 2024 to win back the White House. \n\nHispanics, particularly in Texas and Florida, thought Donald Trump had promised to close the border and focus on deporting only those migrants who were criminals. But unease has spread as ICE crackdowns have targeted a much wider group of Latinos. \n\nThe BBC\u2019s Chief North America Correspondent, Gary O\u2019Donoghue went to Texas to speak to those Latinos and to rural Republicans as they are being urged by the President to vote in these elections for the House and the Senate.\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#USMidterms #BBCNews",
