        "description": "How can you vote in an election if you can't tell what is real?\n\nElections are more impacted by artificial intelligence than ever before, with millions being spent on ads to try and win over voters. \nThis week AI Decoded investigates how artificial intelligence is transforming modern elections, and whether democracy is prepared for the consequences.\n\nJoining us are Oren Etzioni, one of America's leading AI scientists and founder of TrueMedia.org, Sahil Shah, co-founder of Say No to Disinfo, and Priya Lakhani, CEO of Century Tech and a regular contributor to AI Decoded.\n\nIn this video:\n\n0:00 - AI election ads\n7:40 - Who is funding them?\n9:47 - Is it legal?\n12:55 - Can you avoid AI influence?\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#AI #BBCNews",
