        "description": "Nearly 2 million hectares have been torched by wildfires in Indonesia during the country\u2019s worst fire season in a decade. The smoke from these blazes have blanketed the region and its neighbours, such as Malaysia and Singapore, in a thick haze.\n \nThe persistent and toxic conditions have ignited protests across Indonesian cities, with demonstrators demanding President Prabowo Subianto declare the fires a national emergency.\n \nWhile his government is pursuing criminal charges against companies it says are responsible for starting the fires, the blazes continue to burn.\n \nBBC\u2019s Liza Tambunan reports from near the frontline and explains why these wildfires \u2014 which have been supercharged by El Nino \u2014 have been so difficult to extinguish and what life is like for residents living in the smoke.\n \n#Indonesia #wildfires #elnino #asia #BBCNews\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#BBCNews",
